                                         EXHIBIT A



               WITNESS IDENTIFICATION AND QUALIFICATIONS

Q.   Please state your name and business address.

A.   My name is Naomi Koch. My business address is 414 Nicollet Mall, Minneapolis,

     Minnesota 55401.

Q.   On whose behalf are you testifying in this proceeding?

A.   I am filing testimony on behalf of Southwestern Public Service Company, a New Mexico

     corporation (“SPS”) and wholly-owned electric utility subsidiary of Xcel Energy Inc.

     (“Xcel Energy”).

Q.   By whom are you employed and in what position?

A.   I am employed by Xcel Energy Services Inc. (“XES”), the service company subsidiary of

     Xcel Energy, as Director, Tax Reporting.

Q.   Please outline your responsibilities as Director, Tax Reporting.

A.   My duties include overseeing federal and state income, sales/use, and property tax

     compliance and accounting for all Xcel Energy companies.

Q.   Please describe your educational background.

A.   I graduated from the University of Minnesota with a Bachelor of Science degree and a

     Master of Business Taxation degree.

Q.   Please describe your professional experience.

A.   I have over twenty-five years of corporate tax experience with XES and the former

     Northern States Power Company. I joined Northern States Power in 1999 in Tax Services.

     Through this experience, I have become familiar with various provisions of the Internal

     Revenue Code (“IRC”) and Internal Revenue Service (“IRS”) regulations (also referred to

     as rules) that affect public utilities. I also have become familiar with various state laws,


                                              1
                                         EXHIBIT A


     utility commission rules, and court cases that relate to the treatment and calculation of tax

     expenses, including income tax, for ratemaking and utility regulatory purposes, including

     those of New Mexico.

Q.   Have you testified or filed testimony before any regulatory authorities?

A.   Yes. I filed testimony on behalf of SPS before the New Mexico Public Regulation

     Commission (“Commission”) in Case Nos. 15-00296-UT, 17-00255-UT, 19-00170-UT,

     20-00238-UT, and 22-00286-UT, before the Public Utility Commission of Texas in Docket

     Nos. 45524, 47527, 49831, 51802, and 54634, and on behalf of Public Service Company

     of Colorado before the Public Utilities Commission of the State of Colorado in Docket

     Nos. 17AL-0363G, 19AL-0268E, 20AL-0049G, 21AL-0317E, and 22AL-0046G.




